@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Account API
	Testing Koroneiki Account API functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the external links for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" on koroneiki with the following entity id values
	| 1234 |
	| 5678 |
	* I tear down the product purchases on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the following products
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal                      |
	* I tear down the products on koroneiki with the following names
	| Liferay Digital Experience Platform |
	| Liferay Portal                      |
	* I tear down the postal addresses on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following street addresses
	| 123 Fake Street |
	| 456 Main Street |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Automotive |

Scenario: Create and view account with nested fields
	Koroneiki accounts created with nested fields via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a product with the name "Liferay Digital Experience Platform"
	And I generate static start and end dates
	And I create a nested field for the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken"
	And I create a nested field for the account external link with the following values 
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And I create a nested field for the postal address with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91761           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Fake Street |
	And I create a nested field for the product purchase for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	Given I create an account on koroneiki with nested fields with following values
	| Code                          | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Contact Nested Field          | ${staticContactsNestedField}             |
	| Description                   | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| External Link Nested Field    | ${staticAccountExternalLinksNestedField} |
	| Fax Number                    | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry                      | Automotive                               |
	| Name                          | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes                         | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number                  | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Postal Address Nested Field   | ${staticPostalAddressesNestedField}      |
	| Product Purchase Nested Field | ${staticProductPurchasesNestedField}     |
	| Profile Email Address         | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Sold By                       | Liferay US                               |
	| Status                        | Approved                                 |
	| Tier                          | Regular                                  |
	| Website                       | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              | 
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki account with the name "Koroneiki Automotive" and the following values
	| Code                  | KORAUTO                                  |
	| Description           | Test automotive account on koroneiki     |
	| Fax Number            | 555-555-1234                             |
	| Industry              | Automotive                               |
	| Name                  | Koroneiki Automotive                     |
	| Notes                 | Additional account notes                 |
	| Phone Number          | 555-555-5678                             |
	| Profile Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| Sold By               | Liferay US                               |
	| Status                | Approved                                 |
	| Tier                  | Regular                                  |
	| Website               | www.koroneikiautomotive.com              |
	Then the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be assigned the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And the contact with the email address "koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken" should be visible via nested field on the account "Koroneiki Automotive"
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Koroneiki Automotive" for the product "Liferay Digital Experience Platform" via nested field with the following values
	| End Date                | ${staticEndDate}         |                |
	| Original End Date       | ${staticOriginalEndDate} |                |
	| Perpetual               | false                    |                |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp1          | propertyValue1 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp2          | propertyValue2 |
	| Product Field and Value | additionalProp3          | propertyValue3 |
	| Quantity                | 1                        |                |
	| Start Date              | ${staticStartDate}       |                |
	| Status                  | Approved                 |                |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And the external link with the entity id "1234" should be present on the account "Koroneiki Automotive" via the external link key with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And I should be able to view a postal address on koroneiki for the account "Koroneiki Automotive" with the street address "123 Fake Street" with the following values
	| Country               | United States   |
	| Locality              | Diamond Bar     |
	| Region                | California      |
	| Type                  | Business        |
	| Mailing               | True            |
	| Postal Code           | 91761           |
	| Primary               | True            |
	| Street Address Line 1 | 123 Fake Street |

Scenario: Create and view account with nested fields containing multiple entities
	Koroneiki accounts created with nested fields containing multiple entities via API should be viewable via API.

	Given I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Koroneiki                                |
	| Language      | English                                  |
	| Last Name     | Contact1                                 |
	| Middle Name   | User                                     |
	| Okta ID       | koroneikicontact1                        |
	And I create a contact on koroneiki with the following values
	| Email Address | koroneiki.contact2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
